  "body": "Found by the review of PR #2214 (#2210), 2026-11-16.\n\nWhat happens: with PR #2214 the 2D Adaptive operation of `testdata/models/fig8.camproj` generates (6415 moves, 0 gouges). The post is then blocked by 15 warnings \"feed moves cross in XY at shared depth\".\n\nEvidence:\n\n- The reviewer wrote the turn of the part into the part position instead of the setup. The same crossings appear at the same move numbers. Thus the 2D Adaptive generator causes them, not the part alignment of PR #2214.\n- #2237 is the same symptom on 3D Pocket.\n\nExpected: the Adaptive plan for this area does not cross its own feed moves at one depth, or the planner changes to a different pass family for that level. The post is not blocked for a legal program.\n\nSafety: the check and the post block are correct and stay unchanged. The fix is in the generator and changes posted G-code.\n\nDone means: a test generates 2D Adaptive on this shape (two round areas with a narrow neck), verifies with zero crossing warnings, and the post is not blocked. The test names the move numbers that crossed before the fix.\n",
